From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: compat shims for carrying the mainline drm/imagination driver

This tree carries drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/ at mainline level rather than at
the level the 6.18 stable tree ships (see the patch that follows). Two things
mainline's driver uses do not exist here in the form it expects. Both shims live
in this ONE patch, deliberately, so the compatibility surface is a single file
to read and a single patch to delete the day the kernel is bumped.

⚠ EACH IS SMALLER THAN "MISSING API" SUGGESTS, and that is the whole reason
this is viable. The first claim made about them in this session was "core
kernel surgery in three subsystems". That was wrong, and measuring it is what
corrected it:

1. pwrseq -- a RENAME. pwrseq_power_on/off() are present in
   include/linux/pwrseq/consumer.h; mainline calls them pwrseq_enable/disable().
   Aliased rather than editing the driver's two call sites, so the driver stays
   byte-identical to upstream.

2. drm_gpuvm_bo_obtain_locked() -- 26 lines, and every primitive it uses is
   already here: drm_gpuvm_bo_find(), drm_gpuvm_bo_create(),
   drm_gpuvm_immediate_mode(), drm_gem_gpuva_assert_lock_held(). The whole of
   drm_gpuvm.c is 190 lines apart between the two trees (3016 vs 3206).

A third shim, for include/linux/slab.h, left with the bump to 6.18.53.
Mainline's driver calls kmalloc_obj()/kzalloc_obj() and their _objs forms with
the GFP argument left out at 23 of its 24 call sites; on 6.18.36 that argument
was mandatory, so this patch redefined the four macros with an optional one.
Stable 6.18.39 backported the upstream form (2dca62902eb3, "slab: Introduce
kmalloc_flex() and family"; the optional argument goes through default_gfp() in
include/linux/gfp.h), so the stock header takes the short form and a
redefinition would only shadow it. The rest of this patch was regenerated
against 6.18.53 by a 3-way rebase; its hunks are unchanged.

WHAT THIS COSTS US, said plainly: include/linux/pwrseq/consumer.h and
drm_gpuvm.{c,h} differ from pristine 6.18.53. All three hunks are additive and
guarded, and the driver exercises them -- but "additive" is not "harmless". The
widest-reaching part, the slab.h shim included by essentially everything, is
the part that is gone.

VERIFIED: compile-check green with drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/ in the gate.
⚠ NOT hardware-proven.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_gpuvm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_gpuvm.c
index 61c3df0..05cba32 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_gpuvm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_gpuvm.c
@@ -1699,6 +1699,49 @@ drm_gpuvm_bo_obtain(struct drm_gpuvm *gpuvm,
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(drm_gpuvm_bo_obtain);
 
+/**
+ * drm_gpuvm_bo_obtain_locked() - obtains an instance of the &drm_gpuvm_bo for
+ * the given &drm_gpuvm and &drm_gem_object, with the GEM's gpuva lock held
+ * @gpuvm: The &drm_gpuvm the @obj is mapped in.
+ * @obj: The &drm_gem_object being mapped in the @gpuvm.
+ *
+ * COMPAT for the mainline drm/imagination driver this tree carries; the
+ * function is upstream and not in 6.18.36. Reproduced from mainline: every
+ * primitive it needs -- drm_gpuvm_bo_find(), drm_gpuvm_bo_create(),
+ * drm_gpuvm_immediate_mode(), drm_gem_gpuva_assert_lock_held() -- is already
+ * present here, which is why this is 26 lines and not a subsystem port.
+ *
+ * Returns: a pointer to the &drm_gpuvm_bo on success, an ERR_PTR on failure
+ */
+struct drm_gpuvm_bo *
+drm_gpuvm_bo_obtain_locked(struct drm_gpuvm *gpuvm,
+			   struct drm_gem_object *obj)
+{
+	struct drm_gpuvm_bo *vm_bo;
+
+	/*
+	 * In immediate mode this would require the caller to hold the GEMs
+	 * gpuva mutex, but it's not okay to allocate while holding that lock,
+	 * and this method allocates. Immediate mode drivers should use
+	 * drm_gpuvm_bo_obtain_prealloc() instead.
+	 */
+	drm_WARN_ON(gpuvm->drm, drm_gpuvm_immediate_mode(gpuvm));
+
+	vm_bo = drm_gpuvm_bo_find(gpuvm, obj);
+	if (vm_bo)
+		return vm_bo;
+
+	vm_bo = drm_gpuvm_bo_create(gpuvm, obj);
+	if (!vm_bo)
+		return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
+
+	drm_gem_gpuva_assert_lock_held(gpuvm, obj);
+	list_add_tail(&vm_bo->list.entry.gem, &obj->gpuva.list);
+
+	return vm_bo;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(drm_gpuvm_bo_obtain_locked);
+
 /**
  * drm_gpuvm_bo_obtain_prealloc() - obtains an instance of the &drm_gpuvm_bo
  * for the given &drm_gpuvm and &drm_gem_object
diff --git a/include/drm/drm_gpuvm.h b/include/drm/drm_gpuvm.h
index 476990e..39e07e1 100644
--- a/include/drm/drm_gpuvm.h
+++ b/include/drm/drm_gpuvm.h
@@ -726,6 +726,9 @@ struct drm_gpuvm_bo *
 drm_gpuvm_bo_obtain(struct drm_gpuvm *gpuvm,
 		    struct drm_gem_object *obj);
 struct drm_gpuvm_bo *
+drm_gpuvm_bo_obtain_locked(struct drm_gpuvm *gpuvm,
+			   struct drm_gem_object *obj);
+struct drm_gpuvm_bo *
 drm_gpuvm_bo_obtain_prealloc(struct drm_gpuvm_bo *vm_bo);
 
 /**
diff --git a/include/linux/pwrseq/consumer.h b/include/linux/pwrseq/consumer.h
index 7d583b4..03d9012 100644
--- a/include/linux/pwrseq/consumer.h
+++ b/include/linux/pwrseq/consumer.h
@@ -53,4 +53,15 @@ static inline int pwrseq_power_off(struct pwrseq_desc *desc)
 
 #endif /* CONFIG_POWER_SEQUENCING */
 
+/*
+ * COMPAT: mainline renamed pwrseq_power_on/off() to pwrseq_enable/disable()
+ * after 6.18, and the drm/imagination driver this tree carries uses the new
+ * names at two call sites. Aliases rather than editing the driver, so it stays
+ * byte-identical to upstream and the difference sits in one obvious shim.
+ */
+#ifndef pwrseq_enable
+#define pwrseq_enable(desc)	pwrseq_power_on(desc)
+#define pwrseq_disable(desc)	pwrseq_power_off(desc)
+#endif
+
 #endif /* __POWER_SEQUENCING_CONSUMER_H__ */
